        <article id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-32">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-[2rem] border border-neutral-border p-8 sm:p-10 shadow-sm shadow-black/[0.03]">
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-neutral-text-primary border-l-[3px] border-brand-primary pl-4 mb-6">Section 1. Information Collection by WAStays (Jesselton Pixel)</h2>

            <div class="space-y-8 mt-6">
              <section class="group">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-serif text-neutral-text-primary mb-3">General</h3>
                <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-text-secondary leading-relaxed font-medium text-justify">
                  The following sections cover the specifics of each of the three groups from which data may be collected: Visitors, Attendees and Organisers.
                </p>
              </section>

              <section class="group">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-serif text-neutral-text-primary mb-3 flex items-center border-l-[3px] border-brand-primary/30 group-hover:border-brand-primary transition-colors pl-4">1.1 Visitors</h3>
                <div class="text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-3 font-medium text-justify">
                  <p>
                    By visiting our website, you consent to the collection and use of your personal data as described herein. If you do not agree to the terms set out herein, please do not visit this website. If required by applicable law, we will seek your explicit consent to process personal data collected on this website or volunteered by you.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    WAStays may collect, record and analyze information of Visitors to its website including your IP address and cookies. WAStays may also collect and process personal data that you volunteer to us in our website forms, such as when you register for an account, request a demo, submit an enquiry, or sign up for information and newsletters. If you provide WAStays with your social media details, WAStays may retrieve publicly available information about you from those social media services.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Such personal data may comprise your IP address, first and last name, postal and email address, phone number, job title, social network data, areas of interest, and certain information about the company you work for, as well as information regarding the relationship that exists between WAStays and yourself.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    WAStays gathers data about visits to the website, including number of visitors and visits, geo-location data, time spent on the site, pages viewed, features used, and referring website addresses.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <strong class="text-neutral-text-primary">Purpose of Processing Personal Data.</strong>
                    WAStays uses collected data to communicate with Visitors, customize content, improve the website, provide requested services, and analyze how Visitors navigate the site.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <strong class="text-neutral-text-primary">Sharing Personal Data.</strong>
                    WAStays may share such information with service vendors or contractors in order to provide requested services or transactions, or to analyze Visitors' behavior on the website.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <strong class="text-neutral-text-primary">Cookies.</strong>
                    Cookies are small pieces of information sent by a website to a Visitor's hard disk. By continuing to visit the website, you agree to the placement of cookies on your device. If you choose not to accept cookies, we cannot guarantee that your experience will be as complete as it would otherwise be. We may also place cookies from third parties for functional and marketing purposes.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <strong class="text-neutral-text-primary">Links to Other Sites.</strong>
                    While visiting our site, Visitors may follow links to other sites that are beyond our control. WAStays is not responsible for the content or privacy policies of those other sites.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section class="group">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-serif text-neutral-text-primary mb-3 flex items-center border-l-[3px] border-brand-primary/30 group-hover:border-brand-primary transition-colors pl-4">1.2 Attendees</h3>
                <div class="text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-3 font-medium text-justify">
                  <p>
                    Attendees should be aware that in responding to booking registrations, invitations, pre-check-in forms, payment requests, or communication workflows powered by WAStays, they may disclose information that could make them personally identifiable to Organisers. Attendees are responsible for the content of their responses.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    For more detailed information concerning the protection of privacy when responding to any booking or event-related workflow, Attendees may contact the Organiser directly. It is the Organiser's responsibility to ensure that collection and processing of data are done in accordance with applicable law. WAStays will not process personal data of Attendees for purposes other than those instructed by its Organisers.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    If you wish to inquire about personal data collected through forms or workflows powered by WAStays, we recommend that you contact the Organiser that created or sent the relevant form, booking flow, or invitation. As WAStays acts as a processor in many of these cases, it does not control the personal data used or stored, but processes it on behalf of its Organisers.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    During an Attendee's use of WAStays-powered services, information such as name, company name, email, address, phone number, payment information, booking details, and other relevant data may be provided. This information is used by WAStays only as required to identify the Attendee, provide support, fulfil contractual obligations, and carry out services in accordance with the Organiser's instructions.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Attendees' data may include information uploaded, transferred, or manually entered by an Organiser into their account. Personal data may include contact information, family or travel details, age, date of birth, marital status, number of children, employment details, education, business contact details, gender, religion, race, health details and other sensitive personal data where the Organiser has collected such information. Responses to custom questions may also include personal data.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    For Organisers and Attendees in the European Economic Area, the Organiser may be regarded as the controller, while WAStays may be regarded as the processor as those terms are used under the GDPR and related laws.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <section class="group">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-serif text-neutral-text-primary mb-3 flex items-center border-l-[3px] border-brand-primary/30 group-hover:border-brand-primary transition-colors pl-4">1.3 Organisers</h3>
                <div class="text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-3 font-medium text-justify">
                  <p>
                    In order to provide services to its Organisers, WAStays requires the relevant entity to provide pertinent personal data to set up and manage accounts. In addition, WAStays Organisers collect information from Attendees when they publish bookings, registration flows, forms, invitations, or guest communication workflows.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Data entered or transferred into WAStays by Organisers, such as text, questions, contacts, booking details, templates, media files, and operational content, remains the property of the Organiser and may not be shared with a third party by WAStays without the Organiser's express consent, except where required by law or necessary to provide the service.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    During account registration or sign-up, Organisers may provide information such as name, company name, email, address, phone number, payment details, and other relevant data. This information is used by WAStays to identify Organisers and provide support, services, mailings, billing, sales and marketing actions, and to meet contractual obligations.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    If Organisers wish to edit or remove their personal data from WAStays platforms, they may request in writing that WAStays carry out the required actions. WAStays will not retain Organisers' data longer than is necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected or as required by applicable laws or regulations.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </section>
